      "text": "<|begin_of_thought|>\n\nOkay, let's see. I need to find the sum of 929,518 and 947,935. Hmm, adding two big numbers like this can be tricky, but maybe I can break it down into smaller parts to make it easier. Let me start by writing them out:\n\n929,518\n+ 947,935\n----------\n\nFirst, let's line them up by their place values. Since both numbers have the same number of digits, I can add them column by column from right to left. Let me write them again with spaces to make it clearer:\n\n929 518\n+ 947 935\n----------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (the units place):\n\nUnits place: 8 + 5 = 13. So, 13 in the units place. But since we can't have more than 9 in a single place, we need to carry over 1 to the tens place. So, 13 becomes 3 in the units place and 1 in the tens place.\n\nNext, tens place: 1 (from the units carry) + 3 (from 947,935's tens) + 1 (from 929,518's tens) = 5. So, 5 in the tens place.\n\nHundreds place: 5 (from 947,935's hundreds) + 9 (from 929,518's hundreds) = 14. Again, carry over 1 to the thousands place. So, 14 becomes 4 in the hundreds place and 1 in the thousands place.\n\nThousands place: 2 (from 947,935's thousands) + 2 (from 929,518's thousands) = 4. So, 4 in the thousands place.\n\nTen-thousands place: 9 (from 947,935's ten-thousands) + 9 (from 929,518's ten-thousands) = 18. Carry over 1 to the hundred-thousands place. So, 18 becomes 8 in the ten-thousands place and 1 in the hundred-thousands place.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 9 (from 947,935's hundred-thousands) + 9 (from 929,518's hundred-thousands) = 18. Carry over 1 to the million place. So, 18 becomes 8 in the hundred-thousands place and 1 in the million place.\n\nMillion place: 9 (from 947,935's million) + 2 (from 929,518's million) = 11. Carry over 1 to the billion place. So, 11 becomes 1 in the million place and 1 in the billion place.\n\nBillion place: 1 (from 947,935's billion) + 9 (from 929,518's billion) = 10. So, 10 becomes 0 in the billion place and 1 in the trillion place.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the sum is 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1,000,000,000 + 1