      "text": "<|begin_of_thought|>\n\nOkay, let's see. I need to find the sum of 180,375 and 698,507. Hmm, adding two big numbers like this can be tricky, but maybe I can break it down into smaller parts to make it easier. Let me start by writing them out:\n\n180,375\n+698,507\n----------\n\nFirst, I should line up the numbers by their place values. Since both numbers have the same number of digits, I don't need to add extra zeros. Let me write them vertically:\n\n  180,375\n+698,507\n----------\n\nStarting from the rightmost digit (the units place), I'll add each corresponding digit. Let's go step by step.\n\nUnits place: 5 + 7 = 12. So, 12 in the units place. But since we're dealing with whole numbers, we can write down 2 and carry over 1 to the next place.\n\nNext, the tens place: 7 + 0 = 7, plus the carried over 1 makes 8. So, 8 in the tens place.\n\nHundreds place: 3 + 5 = 8, plus the carried over 1 makes 9. So, 9 in the hundreds place.\n\nThousands place: 7 + 8 = 15. Again, 15, so 15 in the thousands place.\n\nTen-thousands place: 0 + 9 = 9, plus the carried over 1 makes 10. So, 10 in the ten-thousands place.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 1 + 6 = 7, plus the carried over 1 makes 8. So, 8 in the hundred-thousands place.\n\nMillions place: 8 + 6 = 14. So, 14 in the millions place.\n\nWait, but let me check if I added the numbers correctly. Let me add them again to make sure I didn't make a mistake.\n\n180,375\n+698,507\n----------\n\nStarting from the right:\n\nUnits: 5 + 7 = 12. 12 in units. 12 - 10 = 2. So, 2 in units.\n\nTens: 7 + 0 = 7. 7 + 1 = 8. So, 8 in tens.\n\nHundreds: 3 + 5 = 8. 8 + 1 = 9. So, 9 in hundreds.\n\nThousands: 7 + 8 = 15. 15 + 1 = 16. So, 16 in thousands.\n\nTen-thousands: 0 + 9 = 9. 9 + 1 = 10. So, 10 in ten-thousands.\n\nHundred-thousands: 1 + 6 = 7. 7 + 1 = 8. So, 8 in hundred-thousands.\n\nMillions: 8 + 6 = 14. 14 + 1 = 15. So, 15 in millions.\n\nWait, but let me verify the sum again. Let's add them step by step:\n\n180,375\n+698,507\n-