(hundreds, carry 1)\n6 + 1 = 7 (thousands)\n2 + 9 = 11 (ten-thousands, carry 1)\n6 + 4 = 10 (hundred-thousands, carry 1)\n0 + 4 = 4 (millions)\n\nSo total sum is 4,000,568. Let me check that again.\n\n4,000,568\n\nBreaking it down:\n\n4,000,000 + 50,000 + 60 + 8 = 4,000,568. Yes, that's correct.\n\nWait, but let me add the numbers again to make sure I didn't make a mistake. Let's add 624,677 and 491,881 step by step.\n\nStarting from the right:\n\n7 + 1 = 8\n\n7 + 8 = 15 (carry 1)\n\n7 + 8 = 15 (carry 1)\n\n6 + 1 = 7\n\n2 + 9 = 11 (carry 1)\n\n6 + 4 = 10 (carry 1)\n\n0 + 4 = 4\n\nSo total sum is 4,000,568. That seems right. But let me check if there's a mistake in the addition.\n\nWait, maybe I should add the numbers differently to verify. Let's add 624,677 + 491,881.\n\nLet me add the numbers column by column:\n\nUnits place: 7 + 1 = 8\n\nTens place: 7 + 8 = 15 (carry 1)\n\nHundreds place: 7 + 8 = 15 (carry 1)\n\nThousands place: 6 + 1 = 7\n\nTen-thousands place: 2 + 9 = 11 (carry 1)\n\nHundred-thousands place: 6 + 4 = 10 (carry 1)\n\nMillions place: 0 + 4 = 4\n\nSo total sum is 4,000,568. That seems correct. But let me check if there's a mistake in the addition.\n\nWait, maybe I made a mistake in the hundreds place. Let's check again:\n\n624,677 + 491,881\n\nAdding the hundreds place: 6 + 1 = 7. Correct.\n\nWait, but maybe I added the hundreds place incorrectly. Let me check again.\n\nWait, 624,677 + 491,881.\n\nAdding the hundreds place: 6 + 1 = 7. Correct.\n\nWait, but maybe I added the hundreds place incorrectly. Let me check:\n\n624,677 + 491,881.\n\nAdding the hundreds place: 6 + 1 = 7. Correct.\n\nWait, but maybe I added the hundreds place incorrectly. Let me check:\n\n624,677 + 491,881.\n\nAdding the hundreds place: 6 + 1 = 7. Correct.\n\nWait, but maybe I added the hundreds place incorrectly. Let me check:\n\n624,677 + 491,881.\n\nAdding the hundreds place: 6 + 1 = 7. Correct.\n\nWait, but maybe I added the hundreds place incorrectly. Let me check:\n\n624,