rs in another way to ensure there's no mistake.\n\nAlternative method: Adding 209,340 + 436,305.\n\nLet me add 209,340 + 400,000 = 609,340\n\nThen add 436,305 to 609,340.\n\nAdding 436,305 to 609,340:\n\nStart from the right:\n\n0 + 5 = 5\n\n4 + 4 = 8\n\n3 + 3 = 6\n\n6 + 0 = 6\n\n9 + 0 = 9\n\n2 + 0 = 2\n\nSo total is 609,340 + 436,305 = 645,645. Same result. So that's consistent. Therefore, the sum is 645,645.\n\n<|end_of_thought|>\n\n<|begin_of_solution|>\n\nTo find the sum of \\(209,340\\) and \\(436,305\\), we align the numbers by their place values and add column by column:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c@{}c@{}c@{}c@{}c@{}c}\n & 2 & 0 & 9 & 3 & 4 & 0 \\\\\n+ & 4 & 3 & 6 & 3 & 0 & 5 \\\\\n\\hline\n & 6 & 4 & 5 & 6 & 4 & 5 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n- **Units place:** \\(0 + 5 = 5\\)\n- **Tens place:** \\(4 + 0 = 4\\)\n- **Hundreds place:** \\(3 + 3 = 6\\)\n- **Thousands place:** \\(9 + 6 = 15\\) (carry over 1)\n- **Ten-thousands place:** \\(0 + 3 = 3\\) (carry over 1)\n- **Hundred-thousands place:** \\(2 + 4 = 6\\)\n\nSumming these results: \\(645,645\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{645645}\n\\]\n\n<|end_of_solution|>",
