\n112,899\n+ 337,961\n= 444,860\n\nYes, that seems right. Let me verify each step again to be thorough.\n\nFirst, adding the ones place: 1 + 1 = 2. Correct.\n\nTens place: 6 + 9 = 15. 15 is 5 in the tens place and carry 1. Correct.\n\nHundreds place: 9 + 8 + 1 = 18. 18 is 8 in the hundreds place and carry 1. Correct.\n\nThousands place: 7 + 2 + 1 = 10. 10 is 0 in the thousands place and carry 1. Correct.\n\nTen-thousands place: 3 + 1 + 1 = 5. Correct.\n\nHundred-thousands place: 3 + 1 = 4. Correct.\n\nMillions place: 3 + 1 = 4. Correct.\n\nSo all the digits add up correctly. The sum is indeed 444,860. I think that's the right answer.\n\n<|end_of_thought|>\n\n<|begin_of_solution|>\n\nTo find the sum of \\(337,961\\) and \\(112,899\\), we align the numbers by their place values and add digit by digit:\n\n\\[\n\\begin{array}{c@{}c@{}c@{}c@{}c@{}c@{}c}\n  & 3 & 3 & 7 & 9 & 6 & 1 \\\\\n+ & 1 & 1 & 2 & 8 & 9 & 9 \\\\\n\\hline\n  & 4 & 4 & 4 & 8 & 6 & 0 \\\\\n\\end{array}\n\\]\n\n- **Ones place**: \\(1 + 1 = 2\\)\n- **Tens place**: \\(6 + 9 = 15\\) (write 5, carry 1)\n- **Hundreds place**: \\(9 + 8 + 1 = 18\\) (write 8, carry 1)\n- **Thousands place**: \\(7 + 2 + 1 = 10\\) (write 0, carry 1)\n- **Ten-thousands place**: \\(3 + 1 + 1 = 5\\)\n- **Hundred-thousands place**: \\(3 + 1 = 4\\)\n- **Millions place**: \\(3 + 1 = 4\\)\n\nSumming all digits: \\(444,860\\).\n\n\\[\n\\boxed{444860}\n\\]\n\n<|end_of_solution|>",
